        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-07T12:43:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree about the badness of global variables, but I don\u0027t see how it\u0027s possible to use Once() instead of a global list: the list is constructed incrementally during the added mutator pass, and the partially constructed list is used by the pass to add dependencies.\n\nI applied some of your suggestions:\n\n- use []string and a global mutex instead of the struct\n- use Once() to provide a getter function for the list",
      "parentUuid": "f4e39e78_1517ce0a",
      "revId": "de3358fdf4e598e6a6a2e1e59616021292f74849",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
